id: pm-h97qxd
title: "Health result contract parity: every checks[] row exposes a boolean ok beside its tri-state status"
description: "GitHub #980 shows that the public health result uses ok:boolean on the envelope but status:ok|warn|fail with no ok property on each checks[] row. Natural agent code reuses row.ok and can report every healthy check as failed or construct a gate that never fires. This is a public SDK result-schema consistency and compatibility issue, not a change to the established meaning of the aggregate health verdict. Duplicate check searched all statuses for health JSON, checks row ok/status, envelope boolean, and the linked GH-785/GH-815 verdict issues; no item owns row-level boolean parity."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[8]: agent-ux,"area:governance","area:sdk",contracts,health,json,safety,typed-output
created_at: "2026-08-11T18:12:41.927Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-11T22:24:01.900Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-11T22:24:01.122Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-11T22:24:01.122Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "The public HealthCheck result type exposes ok:boolean on every checks[] row while preserving status:ok|warn|fail; ok has one documented derivation from status and aggregate advisory/blocking policy remains unchanged; SDK, CLI JSON, MCP, compact/full projections, contracts, fixtures, and docs agree; compatibility tests prove existing status consumers are unchanged and naive row.ok predicates identify failures correctly; packaged npm/npx/bun/bunx acceptance, exact 100/100/100/100 coverage, docstrings, and static gates pass"
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make the public SDK health result self-consistent and safe for naive automation at every nesting level
value: Agents can inspect failing health checks without silently inverting or disabling their gate predicate
impact: "SDK, CLI JSON, MCP, and extension consumers share one backward-compatible truth signal per check"
why_now: The mismatch reproduces in current published packages and lies on the failure-investigation path used by release automation
parent: pm-usfg
reporter: GitHub #980
severity: high
environment: "@unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.7, 2026.8.10, and 2026.8.11; Node 22; Linux"
repro_steps: "Run pm health --json and compare top-level .ok with .checks[0].ok and .checks[0].status; .checks[0].ok is absent while status is ok"
resolution: "Every HealthCheck row now exposes required ok:boolean derived compatibly from its tri-state status across SDK, CLI, MCP, assurance, and projections."
expected_result: "Each checks[] entry carries a boolean ok compatible with the envelope spelling, alongside its existing tri-state status"
actual_result: "The envelope has ok:boolean while each check has only status:string, allowing missing-key falsiness to invert or disable obvious agent gates"
