comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-11T18:12:41.927Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence: all-status searches over health JSON checks row ok/status, envelope boolean, GH-785, and GH-815 found closed SDK health owner pm-oxrw, verdict-policy items pm-83ov2i/pm-r8u2g6/pm-jezo, remediation-map pm-0hnu, and token projection pm-du93sr. Full live metadata confirms those define aggregate semantics, remediation, or projection size; none owns the absent row-level boolean. Canonical external report: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/980."
  "2026-08-11T22:18:16.286Z","harness:codex","Evidence 2026-08-12: every SDK health check row now carries required ok:boolean alongside tri-state status, and CLI JSON, assurance, vector-provider, and projection tests enforce parity. Exact 100/100/100/100 coverage, docstrings/static quality, contracts, packed dogfood, npx, and external-package smoke passed. Temporary acceptance returned ten checks, all with boolean ok and ok === (status === 'ok')."
  "2026-08-11T22:23:33.736Z","harness:codex","Packed Bun acceptance 2026-08-12: npm pack produced unbrained-pm-cli-2026.8.11.tgz and bunx --silent --bun --package <tarball> pm --json --no-extensions contracts --summary exited 0 with schema_version 4.7.0 and 56 command summaries. Registry-backed package-default bunx remains assigned to the post-publish verifier, because Bun does not accept a tarball path in its package-default shorthand."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-11T22:18:16.904Z","harness:codex",Aggregate health truth is insufficient for agents that gate on individual rows; each check must carry a transport-stable boolean while retaining tri-state status for diagnosis.
